{"category": "Added", "changelog_entry": "Enabled support for the Open Knowledge Format (OKF) storage backend, which allows the application to run without Notion credentials, storing results in a local \"docs\" directory by default, and requires explicit output_dir or Notion configuration to maintain compatibility with existing deployments.", "summary": "A new storage backend implements the Open Knowledge Format (OKF) for playlists and videos, persisting summaries as markdown bundles with YAML frontmatter. This enables the application to run without Notion credentials, storing all results in a local \"docs\" directory by default. The CLI now accepts an --output-dir option to select the OKF bundle root. The service layer transparently supports both Notion and OKF backends, updating every configured storage target. BREAKING CHANGE: The CLI and service APIs now require explicit output_dir or Notion configuration. Existing deployments must specify a storage backend.", "version": 1}
